w: This foe with hid- den snares May seize me un- a- wares 
w: Oft in ad- ver- si- ty I know not where to flee; 
w: A fai- ling breath and I In death's strong grasp may lie 
w: They are my sure de- fense, All fear and sor- row, hence! 
w: And by His foot- steps led, My path I safe- ly tread, 
