w: If e'er I fail to watch and pray: I walk in dan- ger all the way. 
w: When storms of woe my soul dis- may, I pass through tri- als all the way. 
w: To face e- ter- ni- ty for aye: Death doth pur- sue me all the way. 
w: Un- harmed by foes, do what they may, I walk 'mongst an- gels all the way. 
w: In spite of ills that threa- ten may, I walk with Je- sus all the way. 
w: For all the world I would not stay, My walk is heav'n- ward all the way.
